WEBVTT

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:08.610
Where am I?

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:16.760
Why... am I here?

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:21.910
Let's see... I was after the black camellia,

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.120
then I tried to help Tsugumi-san...

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.620
Wait, did I die?

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.380
Am I... in that place they call the Underworld?

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:31.980
You're not dead yet.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:37.180
But, in a way,

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:39.220
this is the start of an eternity

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:41.180
more frightening than death.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:42.550
A panda?

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:45.390
I'm a tanuki. What's with that face?

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:49.650
I was just wondering why I was being
 welcomed by such an ugly angel.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.380
Can I continue?

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:54.780
Y-Yes, please.

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:59.280
I'm not an angel, and this
 isn't the Underworld.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.790
You're inside an eternal circuit 
called the black camellia.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:07.040
It's a world of night 
where the sun never rises!

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.770
We're inside the black camellia?

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.270
It's rather large.

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:21.920
That impresses you?

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:24.770
Well, I haven't really come to terms with

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:26.060
being in a clock just yet.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.710
The black camellia stabbed you...

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.960
...and then trapped you here.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.400
Trapped?

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.350
Why do you think the black 
camellia brings bad luck?

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:39.940
Unless someone else is stabbed, 
you can never get out.

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:42.080
Your soul will always grieve.

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:46.080
And how can a miracle like 
good luck come to pass,

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:50.330
when the hands on a clock never 
strike eight simultaneously?

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:53.590
Are you saying that I can...

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:57.840
Right. Good luck is a prayer to someone.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.200
And that prayer is a song, boy.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:07.010
If you sing your heart 
out on this "soul stage,"

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:10.110
the two hands will strike 
eight at the same time.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.640
That's how the black camellia works.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:16.960
But when the song ends, 
your soul will vanish

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:18.950
in exchange for that miracle.

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:24.270
If you want to bless anyone outside with

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.950
fortune in exchange for your life,

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:30.400
you need only get on the stage and sing.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:34.280
And you have to dress like a girl!

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:38.550
Dress like a girl?

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.690
Yes, like a girl.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:46.470
<b><i>Ring the bell of freedom,</i></b>

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:50.140
<b><i>and listen to your heart.</i></b>

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:53.750
<b><i>Don't fear loneliness.</i></b>

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:56.110
<b><i>See? Courage can pierce it in one strike.</i></b>

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:57.160
<b><i>Paradigm Shift.</i></b>

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:01.600
<b><i>Even if you lose sight of everything,</i></b>

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.250
<b><i>Keep walking the path 
where there is no path.</i></b>

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:12.880
<b><i>By burning endless passion.</i></b>

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:18.850
Jeez...

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:22.840
Where could my big sister have gone?

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:25.240
Probably still chasing after her money.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:27.110
Honestly...

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:29.640
By the way, where's Maria-san?

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:34.240
I haven't seen her since she 
walked Nagi-chan to the annex.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:38.190
Give it back!

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:44.110
My black camellia! My beloved!

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.990
Mother! Don't push yourself any more!

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:48.280
Shut up!

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:52.030
Are you no longer grateful for
 being rescued, you thief?

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:56.000
M-Mother...

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.500
Are you all right?

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:02.450
Big sister.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:04.640
Tsugumi.

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:10.720
Whoa!

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:13.330
This has turned into quite 
a situation, Isumi-san.

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:17.110
Yes. I'm finally going 
to put an end to it.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:23.820
Please move.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:26.530
I can't let you pass.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:40.250
Damn.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:44.550
Tsugumi?

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:48.260
Take Mother back to the 
sanctuary, Shidou. Quick!

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:50.030
A-All right.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:54.980
Isumi Saginomiya! I won't 
let you hurt my mother!

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:58.610
Hey, hey! Now's not the time to fight.

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:04.260
My mother saved me from the desert 
where I was abandoned and raised me!

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:09.130
Even if she only did it to have 
me search for the black camellia,

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.450
she's still my mother to me!

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:14.540
Isumi-san!

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:20.380
Isumi-san?

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:22.710
Are you all right, Isumi-san?

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:26.290
All right, then.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:30.970
I will show you what Hell is like.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:32.960
<i>Oh no, she's lost it...</i>

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:37.190
Hey, little one! 
You better run!

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:38.020
Huh?

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:47.370
Are you all right?

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:49.070
Father!

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.550
The black camellia...

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:55.040
Give me back my black camellia!

00:05:55.850 --> 00:06:01.790
Never! Hayate is in here... 
Someone very important to me is in here!

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:06.940
No! The person in there is...

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:09.390
the one that I love!

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:16.180
Come on!

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:20.600
Wait!

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:26.380
No, Dolly. Your body won't 
last. We have to go back.

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:27.440
Shut up!

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:38.360
Don't you move.

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:42.200
Hurry up, boss!

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:44.100
The money is in the helicopter.

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:45.800
We can fly any time.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:49.750
So, we'll be taking the money now. Thank you!

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:51.800
You're coming with us.

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:53.430
Oh, no!

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:54.600
What is it?

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:56.880
I think... I just lost the

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:59.950
three million dollar ring Ruka gave back to me!

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:01.990
What? You've gotta be kidding!

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:03.660
What? What is it?

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:05.230
I lied.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:13.270
Nice!

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:15.580
Never underestimate the
 Sanzenin household's maid.

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:18.080
If you do, you'll get hurt!

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:20.740
Were you okay, Maria-san?

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:23.000
Yes. I'm sorry to have 
caused so much trouble.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:24.460
Hey, what's the hold up?

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:27.580
You're the only one left!

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:28.450
To hell...

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:30.000
...with the hostage!

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:31.350
What the...?

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:46.400
Hey, what's going on?

00:07:47.350 --> 00:07:49.320
Hina! Why are you here?

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:52.050
I was worried, of course!

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:54.310
Anyway, it's really dangerous here.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:56.410
Where are you going?

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.240
Nagi is still upstairs, right?

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:00.040
Y-Yes.

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:04.920
I'll go check, so take Maria-san 
somewhere safe, big sister.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.420
What? But my money...

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:11.260
There are more important 
things than money!

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:12.420
Now, hurry and go!

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:15.430
A-A-A-All right! Jeez!

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:16.880
Let's go.

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:17.930
Thanks.

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:24.650
Wow.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.340
"Wow," nothing!

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:28.150
You went totally overboard!

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:33.090
What was the point of doing that to an old 
man you don't even know, or the little one?

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:37.750
I had to sacrifice the old man 
in order to win the battle.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:39.240
Liar!

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:41.200
You have to think of the others...

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:43.540
Watch out!

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:44.750
White Cherry Blossom!

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:49.710
Are you okay?

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:51.840
Student council president.

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:54.760
I'm not sure what happened, but we have

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.500
to get her to the hospital, quick!

00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:58.620
But Nagi is...

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:01.470
No, Isumi-san. This is urgent.

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:05.770
I'll take care of Nagi.

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:06.770
You take care of her.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:08.190
O-Okay.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:11.610
This way. Hurry!

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:16.360
Is the guy trapped in 
there really important?

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:20.220
Yes. He's always there 
for me when I'm in trouble.

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:22.950
He's kind and reliable.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:28.750
He can be a bit clumsy, but all of him 
is important to me, including that!

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:31.380
I see.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:34.510
The helicopter. Let's escape!

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:36.730
Can you fly it?

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:38.220
I'm a butler!

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:41.330
I can even fly a fighter jet!

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:43.790
Really? Then hurry and fly it!

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:44.300
What?

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:45.370
Teacher!

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:47.850
What are you doing, big sister?

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.100
I told you to get out of here!

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:52.260
I-I helped Maria-san escape.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:56.650
So I... My money... Um...

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:02.830
Hurry! Get in! We're leaving!

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.390
Come on, Hina!

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:07.620
You too, Nagi.

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:16.550
Stop, Dolly!

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:17.930
Nagi!

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:22.940
Nagi!

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:54.230
Wow! Awesome!

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:55.960
That's America for you.

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:11.480
If you don't want to be crushed,

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:13.810
then hand over the black camellia.

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:17.030
Are you stupid?

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:18.650
What?

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:22.470
If you were in my position,

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:25.120
would <i>you</i> hand over the black camellia?

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:29.290
Of course not!

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:32.080
He's more important 
to me than my own life!

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:33.960
Nagi!

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:36.930
Father!

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:37.840
Let's go!

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:40.050
Insolent brats!

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:47.950
You have a parachute on, right?

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:48.780
What?

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:51.080
Hurry! We won't last!

00:11:51.470 --> 00:11:52.980
Hina, this way!

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:56.480
B-Big sister...

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:02.920
There are more important 
things than money!

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:05.450
Let's go.

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:16.200
Father!

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:20.020
The nuisance is gone.

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:24.970
Now give back the black camellia.

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:30.290
Give me back my beloved who's within it!

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:33.230
Stop making me repeat myself!

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:40.300
The person in here is someone 
very important to me, Hayate Ayasaki!

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:42.450
Then...

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:45.320
I will twist and crush you to death!

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:49.160
<i>Hayate!</i>

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:54.710
You want the black camellia back?

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:58.040
Father?

00:13:01.350 --> 00:13:03.550
Give me that!

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:08.460
That's...

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:13.360
I grabbed it before you 
were taken away. Sorry.

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:16.440
I've a favor to ask, Nagi.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:23.900
If you could find my stolen wedding 
ring after this, I'd appreciate it.

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:26.410
You want this, Dolly?

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:32.660
Then there happens to be a good way 
to prove that your beloved has died!

00:13:35.860 --> 00:13:37.940
Watch carefully, Dolly.

00:13:37.940 --> 00:13:41.260
Let's see whose beloved
 comes out, yours or Nagi's!

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:42.380
This is your answer!

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:50.570
Don't make that face.

00:13:51.550 --> 00:13:52.850
Father...

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:56.920
That cute face you got from Yukariko...

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:59.770
is wasted... like that...

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:03.520
Father! Father!

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:06.680
Father!

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:11.660
Yo.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.290
And you are?

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:23.070
That's not important. What matters is...

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:27.520
My daughter is in trouble.

00:14:27.520 --> 00:14:30.470
You have to help her 
once you're out of here.

00:14:30.940 --> 00:14:33.550
Huh? Um, sure.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:45.110
I'll leave it to you.

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:47.010
Wait...

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:51.920
I've kept a lady waiting.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:02.300
I have no further need for you!

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:09.260
Oh, my beloved.

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:10.600
My king...

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:14.910
It's me... Your Dryad.

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:33.620
Thanks for waiting, Miss Nagi.

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:35.120
Hayate!

00:15:40.930 --> 00:15:41.920
Why...

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:45.280
Why aren't you looking at me after

00:15:45.280 --> 00:15:46.840
being stabbed by the black camellia?

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:52.840
Why are you not showering 
me with your kind words?

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:15.950
Hayate! If we fall from up here...

00:16:18.390 --> 00:16:19.750
You're right.

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:23.830
There's no way we'd survive
 under normal circumstances.

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:24.670
What?

00:16:25.070 --> 00:16:25.920
But...

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:30.510
Never let go of my hand, 
no matter what, Miss Nagi.

00:16:36.860 --> 00:16:38.350
Hayate!

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:43.970
Don't worry. I'm sure your 
father will protect us.

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:55.700
See?

00:16:57.760 --> 00:16:59.080
Hayate...

00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:03.080
I'm sorry I was late, Miss Nagi.

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:05.180
Hayate!

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:09.780
<i>Will you be my butler?</i>

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:12.510
<i>As promised, shall we do some 
stargazing here together?</i>

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:14.940
<i>Hayate! Hurry and do something!</i>

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:16.840
<i>Do you like me, Hayate?</i>

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:17.620
<i>Hayate!</i>

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:18.290
<i>Hayate!</i>

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:19.690
<i>Hayate!</i>

00:17:19.690 --> 00:17:22.820
<i>I'll always protect you, 
in both the past and the future.</i>

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:24.760
<i>I'll protect you.</i>

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:27.940
Hayate!

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:29.270
Yes?

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:34.280
I... I really like you, Hayate!

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:38.990
I like you more than anyone in the whole world!

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:42.830
So... So...

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:46.530
Thank you.

00:17:46.530 --> 00:17:51.390
That's something very special, 
so we'll have to cherish it.

00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:55.160
Yes!

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:03.300
It's raining money. You don't care?

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:06.810
Nope. I won some once.

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:09.740
So I'll win some again!

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:18.070
Mother.

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:21.860
I wonder if Nagi and the 
gang are all right.

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:23.080
They are.

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:26.370
A miracle protects them.

00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:46.480
Yukkyun.

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:49.850
That was an amazing performance.

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:52.640
Oh... That's right.

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:04.120
I've made you wait.

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.120
Yes.

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:16.210
We're safe.

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:17.090
Yes.

00:19:25.490 --> 00:19:26.600
Dolly!

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:29.310
Miss Nagi!

00:19:31.570 --> 00:19:32.620
Dolly...

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:39.540
My mother told me that...

00:19:40.020 --> 00:19:42.440
...that man left you a message before

00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:44.030
he died in the accident.

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:50.290
<i>Thank you, Dolly. I love you.</i>

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:07.520
Miss Nagi...

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:11.270
Do you think he was able 
to go without getting lost?

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:13.370
I'm not sure.

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:18.030
But regret is always a part of life.

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:19.880
Yeah...

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:21.030
That's true.

00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:25.990
Looks like Ruka-san is back for her encore.

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:28.540
Let's go watch!

00:22:01.430 --> 00:22:04.130
Here. It's your wedding ring.

00:22:06.920 --> 00:22:09.230
The black camellia hasn't 
moved since then.

00:22:09.230 --> 00:22:11.470
It won't bring bad luck, 
even if we hold on to it.

00:22:11.960 --> 00:22:14.480
Thanks for helping us.

00:22:16.080 --> 00:22:18.250
Still, that was amazing!

00:22:18.250 --> 00:22:19.400
What was?

00:22:20.020 --> 00:22:21.710
Didn't Teacher Katsura

00:22:21.710 --> 00:22:25.230
overcome that bad luck and 
end up winning 1.2 billion yen?

00:22:25.230 --> 00:22:27.850
But that happiness was fleeting,

00:22:27.850 --> 00:22:29.960
since she doesn't have the money anymore.

00:22:29.960 --> 00:22:32.990
That's a sort of bad luck. Besides...

00:22:33.510 --> 00:22:35.960
If she had succumbed 
to the allure of money,

00:22:35.960 --> 00:22:39.500
she could have lost her 
precious little sister.

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:41.500
You're right.

00:22:41.860 --> 00:22:45.780
But something else has been
 bothering me even more.

00:22:45.780 --> 00:22:46.510
What?

00:22:46.950 --> 00:22:50.510
Your mother may have died

00:22:50.980 --> 00:22:56.310
with the mistaken impression that 
your father may have had an affair...

00:22:57.600 --> 00:23:01.520
Oh, I wouldn't worry much about that.

00:23:02.080 --> 00:23:03.440
Why?

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:08.450
When you're faced with bad luck, there's 
bound to be a misunderstanding or two.

00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:12.450
Mistakes and sad things will happen...

00:23:14.350 --> 00:23:17.400
But real love doesn't succumb to misfortune.

00:23:19.170 --> 00:23:21.050
So they're fine.

00:23:22.430 --> 00:23:23.730
You're right.

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:31.650
Gosh, I'm starving!

00:23:31.650 --> 00:23:34.060
What's for dinner, Hayate?

00:23:34.060 --> 00:23:36.720
Salisbury steak, Miss Nagi.
